) 60.\",\n      \"The official answer table lists 法規 問13(b) = 5. The candidate officialAnswer is also 5.\",\n      \"Equivalent circuit: the 100 V source feeds Rb = 40 Ω in series with Rd in parallel with Rh = 6000 Ω. The current-division result Ih = 100Rd/[Rb(Rd+Rh)+RdRh] = 100Rd/(6040Rd+240000) is algebraically correct.\",\n      \"Setting Ih = 0.01 A gives 39.6Rd = 2400, so Rd ≈ 60.6 Ω. Checking Rd = 60 Ω gives 6000/602400 ≈ 9.96 mA, which confirms it.\",\n      \"Approximate method: the case voltage is 100Rd/(40+Rd) ≤ 6000 × 0.01 = 60 V, so Rd ≤ 60 Ω. This agrees with choice (5).\",\n      \"Body currents for each choice recalculated: Rd = 10 Ω gives 1000/300400 ≈ 3.33 mA. Rd = 15 Ω gives 1500/330600 ≈ 4.54 mA. Rd = 20 Ω gives 2000/360800 ≈ 5.54 mA. Rd = 30 Ω gives 3000/421200 ≈ 7.12 mA. All match the stated values.\",\n      \"The only Interpretation-based input is Rb = 40 Ω from (a), which is confirmed on page 32 (Article 17, table 17-1). The explanation makes no other independent claims about the Interpretation.\",\n      \"The original has no figure. The explanation describes the equivalent circuit well enough to follow without one, and figureUrls is empty, which is appropriate.\"\n    ]\n  }\n]\n```","ttft_ms":29237,"type":"result","duration_ms":42234,"uuid":"ac166a5d-b2ca-41d3-9f9f-87cfc3aeb1b7","ttft_stream_ms":2642,"time_to_request_ms":145,"first_content_frame_ms":2642,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
